// `[package] root` is the segment a package's modules derive under, declared separately from its
// `[package] name`. This case's identity is `noeta-lang/my-toolkit` — a registry coordinate whose
// halves no `use` could spell — and `root = "toolkit"` says what its files derive under instead.
//
// So `text.noe` is the module `toolkit.text`, imported by that name. Separating the two is what
// lets an identity look like the forge name it already is while every import stays a legal
// identifier; without the `root`, this manifest is refused for exactly that reason.
// expect: stdout "HI ada"
// expect: exit 0
use toolkit.text.shout;

echo "${shout("hi")} ada"
